<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Unknown component from a magnitude</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(P({@P[1]@},\,{@P[2]@},\,{@P[3]@})\) and \(Q({@q1@},\,{@q2@},\,k)\). The distance \(PQ\) is \({@dd@}\).</p><p>Find the two possible values of \(k\).</p><div>\(k =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] or \(k =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</div><div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(\overrightarrow{PQ} = \begin{pmatrix} {@dx@} \\ {@dy@} \\ {@zc@} \end{pmatrix}\), so \(({@dx@})^2 + ({@dy@})^2 + ({@zc@})^2 = {@dd@}^2\).</p><p>Then \(({@zc@})^2 = {@dd^2@} - {@dx^2+dy^2@} = {@s^2@}\), so \({@zc@} = \pm {@s@}\), giving \(k = {@r1@}\) or \(k = {@r2@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: an unknown component from a magnitude; the three sets are distinct on every entry (P[3] # 0). Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 4, Chapter 9, Exercise D, Q8. */
klist: [[[-3,-1,3],[-4,-3],3,2],[[-4,2,-2],[2,8],11,7],[[-2,2,-2],[-3,6],9,8],[[-4,3,-4],[-8,-1],9,7],[[4,5,-2],[2,11],11,9],[[5,-4,1],[-1,2],11,7],[[4,5,6],[7,9],13,12],[[2,4,1],[4,9],15,14],[[-4,-1,-5],[-6,9],15,11],[[-5,-4,-5],[-4,-12],9,4]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
P: klist[ix][1]; q1: klist[ix][2][1]; q2: klist[ix][2][2]; dd: klist[ix][3]; s: klist[ix][4];
p3: P[3]; dx: q1-P[1]; dy: q2-P[2];
r1: p3+s; r2: p3-s;
roots: {r1, r2}; dg1: {s, -s}; dg2: {-p3+s, -p3-s};
zc: k-p3;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>ix={@ix@}, d={@dd@}, roots {@roots@}</text>
  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Vectors II: unknown component from a magnitude</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.6: Find both values of an unknown coordinate from the distance between two points in three dimensions.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question 8 in Exercise D of Chapter 9 of Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 4 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2005: new points and distances, both values in either order, randomised over a curated list, with named feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
